Job Title: Oracle Cloud Project Coordinator (Remote)
Location: Nashville, TN (Local candidates preferred)
Duration: 6 Months
Interview: Virtual

Role Summary:
Support the Oracle Cloud program team during post-implementation stabilization across HCM, ERP, Payroll, and Pension systems serving approximately 26,000 employees.
Key Responsibilities:
•	Schedule meetings, prepare agendas, record minutes, and track action items.
•	Maintain project documentation, issue logs, trackers, schedules, and status reports.
•	Coordinate vendor communications, steering committee meetings, and leadership updates.
•	Track project milestones, deliverables, deadlines, and workstreams.
•	Assist with budget tracking, vendor invoices, contract hours, and financial reports.
•	Support vendor onboarding, meeting logistics, and general program administration.
Required Skills:
•	Strong organization, attention to detail, and follow-through.
•	Experience in project coordination or administrative support.
•	Ability to manage multiple priorities and workstreams.
•	Proficiency in Microsoft Office, Teams, and SharePoint.
•	Strong written and verbal communication skills.
•	Ability to work independently and take initiative.
Preferred Skills:
•	Enterprise software or ERP implementation experience.
•	Smartsheet, Jira, or similar project management tools.
•	Public sector or government experience.
•	Vendor invoice review and contract financial tracking.

